<title>PERU: Peru's September copper output rises 14.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Peru's September copper output rises 14.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's copper output rose 14.1 percent to 39,326 tonnes in September compared with the same month last year, according to preliminary figures from the Energy and Mines Ministry released Tuesday.</p>
<p>Production rose 20.6 percent to 355,363 tonnes in the first nine months of the year compared with the same period last year, the ministry said.</p>
<p>In 1995, copper output rose 10.8 percent to 404,990 tonnes from 365,513 tonnes in 1994.</p>
<p>Peru is the world's sixth largest copper producer. The country's largest producer, Southern Peru Copper Corp, accounts for around 60 percent of the country's output.</p>
<p>-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134</p>
</text>
